            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "schemas/gpio_presence.json",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "You need to add the `LogPresenceChange` property to `required` array here as well\notherwise configurations are not required to provide the property.\n\nIf there are configurations without the property then EM will not expose it on D-Bus and create the interface with a different set of properties, which is not allowed in D-Bus.\n\nIt will also cause errors and exceptions in PDI clients trying to read the missing property."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/gpio-presence/device_presence.cpp",
                    "line": 114,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't belong in gpio-presence.  It belongs in entity-manager itself as the probes occur.  I think someone else already has a patch for that, don't they?\n\nThe reason this doesn't belong here is because the DEVICE_NAME path is a dbus-path that is suppose to be \"private\" between the presence daemon and entity-manager and it has no correlation to a Redfish URI.  Therefore we can never add proper translation from the Argument to a valid Redfish URI.\n\nConversely, entity-manager paths usually have a corresponding Redfish URI; so we can [eventually] add valid Argument mapping in bmcweb for those dbus-path to URI translations (which are supposed to be done per the Redfish standard)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/gpio-presence/device_presence.cpp",
                    "line": 117,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Don't make a journal log for something you've already made an event for.  This isn't useful.  Especially because most of the time phosphor-logging is already splatting stuff to the journal."
                }
            ],
